 "input": "blood donation session at the church hall. donors book an appointment in the app. on arrival, reception checks them in and gives the health questionnaire. nurse does the private health screening chat and the finger prick haemoglobin test. if ok, donor goes to the chair and the donor carer does the donation, ~10 mins, bag labelled with the donation barcode. rest and snacks for 15 mins at the refreshment table. bags go in cool boxes and the driver takes them to the processing centre that evening, where they're tested and separated. donor records updated with the barcode so test results link back.",
